// E027: the thunk-list fan.race was removed in 0.42.0; the name returned in
// Stage 3 as a deterministic BLOCK HEAD, renamed fan.min in dialect epoch 14
// (fan.min(compute.ms(5)) { a(), b() } — least deterministic computation
// within the budget wins, ties to source order; the clock is required). The
// legacy call form still gets this signature-migration tombstone.
//
// Almide's concurrency model is deterministic data-parallelism (the answer to #1000,
// docs/roadmap/active/concurrency-stance.md): `fan` may execute in parallel, but
// observable behaviour is defined to be sequential evaluation in LIST ORDER. A
// combinator named for "first to complete wins" has no meaning in that model.
//
// It never raced anyway — the desugar replaced `fan.race([t0, t1, …])` with t0's body
// and never evaluated the rest, so it was a no-op wrapper whose name was its only
// contribution. SPEC.md sold it as a race while contract C-004 documented list order;
// the prose was the part that was wrong.
effect fn a() -> Result[String, String] = ok("a")

effect fn b() -> Result[String, String] = ok("b")

effect fn main() -> Unit = {
  let w = fan.race([
    () => a(),
    () => b()
  ])
  match w {
    ok(v) => println(v),
    err(e) => println(e),
  }
}
